:: OC Bobby Intro 2 Driven [nobr]

<<set $Minutes += 10>>
The drive only takes a few minutes and you go the exact way <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> described. Turning towards the schools, then going far past the high school. The residential houses and shops soon give way to long stretches of empty fields, lone houses on a range, or impressively maintained farmlands. You have brief memories of driving past here when first moving to town, but you still had no idea such rural farmland was so close! <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> notices you staring out the window and smiles. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Yup, it’s pretty beautiful out here. You know, Opal City used to be a bunch of different smaller towns, lots of ‘em farming communities. So, there’s quite a few of us still around.”</span> He explains before turning onto a dirt road that leads to one such farm. You pass by a sign that says, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thompson’s Farm”</span> and park just in front of the large wooden farm house out front. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Welcome to the farm!”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> laughs, putting the truck in park and exiting the vehicle. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Let me give you the grand tour!”</span> <br>
<br>
<<include"OC Bobby Intro 2">>

:: OC Bobby Intro 2 Walked [nobr]

<<set $Minutes += 30>>
When you set out from the High School in the direction of the farms, you had no idea just how long of a walk it would be. Expecting a brief stroll, <span style="color:Yellow">you are instead greeted by a grueling 45-minute walk that leaves your feet burning and your legs tired.</span> You really should have taken <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> up on his offer to drive you or at least taken the bus. Despite the long walk, however, you do seem to be going in the right direction as the residential houses and shops soon give way to long stretches of empty fields, lone houses on range, and impressively maintained farmlands. <br>
<br>
Then you finally see it, the sign introducing <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Thompson’s Farm”</span>. You’ve made it! Walking up the dirt road leading up to the large farmhouse, you spot <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> out front moving some boxes. He smiles upon seeing you and runs over. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Well know, wasn’t sure you were going to make it. Great to see you!”</span> He laughs, patting you on the head, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Alright then, let me give you the grand tour!”</span> <br>
