:: OC Bobby Intro 2 [nobr]

The first thing <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> shows you is the large house you are standing in front of. It is a sizeable wood and stone structure with a rustic yet homely feel. While no Avendale, it is clear that <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span>’s family is pretty well off. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“This is the house and also the only place with air conditioning.”</span> He laughs, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Feel free to hang out in the living room if you need a break. Also always have cold water and juice in the fridge, so feel free to help yourself. Staying hydrated is important. Bathroom is down this way on the right. Farm work can be pretty swetty, so you can have a shower afterwards if you want. I’m really the only one that uses this bathroom, so you don’t have to worry about my family walking in on you.”</span> <br>

       <<set _ad to [
        {
            Name: "Player",
            State: {
                Mouth: "Happy",
            },
        },
      {
            Name: "OC Bobby",
            State: {
                Outfit: "Everyday",
                Mouth: "Happy",
                },
            },
        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

Walking back outside, you marvel at just how large the farm is. Outside of the large farmhouse behind you, there are two other main features. First is the nearby barn, a large classically red barn surrounded by animal pens. Walking towards it causes the smell of animals to become stronger and, while a little gross, you quickly get used to it. There you can see a large mixture of chickens, cows, pigs, and even a few horses penned away. <span style="color:Pink">You blush a little when <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> offers to maybe show you how to ride sometimes.</span> <br>
<br>
The last feature of the farms is the large fields that seem to stretch on for miles. There is a large variety of fruit and vegetables, it seems they grow just about everything here and you feel a little overwhelmed by just how much there is. You can see why they need the help! The largest field is an orchard full of trees doted with orange dots, which you’d imagine are likely oranges. The scent from these trees travels far and gives the entire place a pleasant, citrusy smell. <br>
<br>
<span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“And that’s everything, pretty much.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> says as the tour finishes, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“We normally need help all over the farm, so I’m sure we’ll be posting a large variety of stuff on the job board. May be a bit of a trek, but we’ll pay you enough to make the bus fare worth it.”</span> He laughs, stretching his arms into the air, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Since you’re here, want to try it out? I’ll even let you choose where you wanna work.”</span> <span style="color:Yellow">You ponder which of the locations you’d like to spend your time.</span> <br>
<br>
<div id="choice">
    <<requiresTrait "Flirty" "Work in the House">>
    <<replace"#choice">>
        With a smirk, you ask if any work needs done in the house. <span style="color:Pink">Maybe if <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> needs a shower you could help him out there. Wash those hard-to-reach places.</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Bobby</span> laughs at your comment, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“That’s not exactly the type of help we’re hiring for. Besides, I got long arms, so I’m pretty good at reaching all the spots. I meant more so with the animals or crops.”</span> He pats you on the head wholesomely and you get the feeling he didn’t catch that you were trying to flirt or just changed the subject. Alas, maybe another time. <br>
        <br>
    <</replace>>
    <</requiresTrait>>
</div>
